<exercisegroup cols="2" xml:id="exercisegroup-orthog-proj-Rn">
<title>Orthogonal projection in <m> \R^n </m></title>

<introduction><p>
	In each case:
	<ol>

		<li> Compute <m> \uproj{u}{a} </m>. </li>

		<li><p>
			Express <m> \uvec{u} </m> as a decomposition into a sum of its
			<term><xref ref="definition-orthog-parallel-component" text="custom">vector component parallel to <m> \uvec{a} </m></xref></term>
			and its
			<term><xref ref="definition-orthog-orthog-component" text="custom">vector component orthogonal to <m> \uvec{a} </m></xref></term>.
		</p></li>

	</ol>
</p></introduction>

<exercise>

	<statement><p>
		<m> \uvec{u} = ( -1, 3,  1) </m>,
		<m> \uvec{a} = (  5, 5, -4) </m>
	</p></statement>

	<answer><p><ol>

		<li><m> \uproj{u}{a} = (5/11, 5/11, -4/11) </m></li>

		<li><p>
			<m> \uvec{u} = \uvec{p} + \uvec{n} </m>,
			where <m> \uvec{p} = \uproj{u}{a} </m> as already computed,
			and <md> \uvec{n} = \uvec{u} - \uvec{p} = (-16/11, 28/11, 15/11) </md>.
		</p></li>

	</ol></p></answer>

</exercise>

<exercise>

	<statement><p>
		<m> \uvec{u} = (  6,  0, 4) </m>,
		<m> \uvec{a} = ( -5, -1, 5) </m>
	</p></statement>

	<answer><p><ol>

		<li><m> \uproj{u}{a} = (50/51, 10/51, -50/51) </m></li>

		<li><p>
			<m> \uvec{u} = \uvec{p} + \uvec{n} </m>,
			where <m> \uvec{p} = \uproj{u}{a} </m> as already computed,
			and <md> \uvec{n} = \uvec{u} - \uvec{p} = (256/51, -10/51, 254/51) </md>.
		</p></li>

	</ol></p></answer>

</exercise>

<exercise>

	<statement>
		<p><m> \uvec{u} = ( 0, -2,  6,  0) </m></p>
		<p><m> \uvec{a} = ( 1, -2, -6, -1) </m></p>
	</statement>

	<answer><p><ol>

		<li><m> \uproj{u}{a} = (-16/21, 32/21, 32/7, 16/21) </m></li>

		<li><p>
			<m> \uvec{u} = \uvec{p} + \uvec{n} </m>,
			where <m> \uvec{p} = \uproj{u}{a} </m> as already computed,
			and <md> \uvec{n} = \uvec{u} - \uvec{p} = (16/21, -74/21, 10/7, -16/21) </md>.
		</p></li>

	</ol></p></answer>

</exercise>

<exercise>

	<statement>
		<p><m> \uvec{u} = (  3, 4, -5, -1, 2) </m></p>
		<p><m> \uvec{a} = ( -1, 4,  0,  2, 6) </m></p>
	</statement>

	<answer><p><ol>

		<li><m> \uproj{u}{a} = (-23/57, 92/57, 0, 46/57, 46/19) </m></li>

		<li><p>
			<m> \uvec{u} = \uvec{p} + \uvec{n} </m>,
			where <m> \uvec{p} = \uproj{u}{a} </m> as already computed,
			and <md> \uvec{n} = \uvec{u} - \uvec{p} = (194/57, 136/57, -5, -103/57, -8/19) </md>.
		</p></li>

	</ol></p></answer>

</exercise>

</exercisegroup>
